m25p80: clear the write enable latch when a program or erase completes

A NOR flash resets WEL at the end of every Page Program, Sector / Block /
Chip Erase (the datasheets of every part in the table); the model left
it set until a WRDI or WRSR.  Drivers that wait for SR to read neither
WIP nor WEL after an operation, as the Fullhan 3.0.8 kernels' m25p80
fork does (wait_till_ready(): sr & (SR_WIP | SR_WEL)), then time out
after 40 seconds on every erase and program -- JFFS2 put each freshly
erased block on its bad list.  Clear the latch when the erase is done
and when the select rises on a page program.

---
diff --git a/hw/block/m25p80.c b/hw/block/m25p80.c
index a5336d9..84799a3 100644
--- a/hw/block/m25p80.c
+++ b/hw/block/m25p80.c
@@ -647,6 +647,8 @@ static void flash_erase(Flash *s, int offset, FlashCMD cmd)
     }
     memset(s->storage + offset, 0xff, len);
     flash_sync_area(s, offset, len);
+    /* The erase is done at once, and with it the write enable latch. */
+    s->write_enable = false;
 }
 
 static inline void flash_sync_dirty(Flash *s, int64_t newpage)
@@ -1550,6 +1552,10 @@ static int m25p80_cs(SSIPeripheral *ss, bool select)
         if (s->state == STATE_COLLECTING_VAR_LEN_DATA) {
             complete_collecting_data(s);
         }
+        /* Deselecting starts the program, which clears WEL as it ends. */
+        if (s->state == STATE_PAGE_PROGRAM) {
+            s->write_enable = false;
+        }
         s->len = 0;
         s->pos = 0;
         s->state = STATE_IDLE;
